ssemination of scientific research, challenging traditional publishing models dominated by subscription-based journals. Key figures such as Peter J. Murray-Rust, one of the founding members, played a crucial role in establishing PLOS's mission to ensure that research is freely available to the public, thus democratizing access to knowledge across the globe.

